# Bluetooth auto-off option (patches/bt_auto_off/README.md): turn
# Bluetooth off after 10 minutes without a connection instead of 5.
name: bt-auto-off-10min
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x030661e0
gate: build refuses unless the stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`; at most one bt-auto-off patch per build (build.py
  --bt-auto-off); the finished image must pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale:
  Module 0's Bluetooth supervisor (0x03065FD4) checks, while
  Bluetooth is on (SAVEINFO +0x2D4) and no device is connected (+0x2D3,
  set to 1 by the module's 'CQ..O' link reply and to 0 by 'S', 'L', 'I'
  or a 'CT' frame), whether the 10 ms tick at 0x03023298 has passed the
  last-connected timestamp by more than 30,000 ticks (movw r1, #0x7530
  at 0x030661E0; bls.w at 0x030661E6). If so it clears event flag 0x1CB,
  clears +0x2D3 and +0x2D4, and powers the module down, so Bluetooth
  turns itself off after 5 minutes without a connection and the saved
  setting reads Off. The tick unit is pinned by the screen-off timer at
  0x03064A1E, which scales its table of seconds by 100 against the
  same counter.
  This patch raises the limit to 60,000 ticks (10 minutes), the largest
  movw immediate that is a whole number of minutes. Nothing else in the
  supervisor changes.
expect: 47f23051
replace: 4ef66021
